IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-business-formulas`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997, ss 40-70, 40-72, 40-75, 328-190(1) -- worked cases for itaa-business-formulas.l4
-- (24 October 2026).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected results were worked by hand from
-- the text and the formulas transcribed in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.formulas.md, before the encoding was run.
-- The first case is the Act's own Example to s 40-75; the rest are hypothetical.

§ `s 40-75 -- prime cost`

-- The s 40-75 Example: "Greg acquires an asset for $3,500 and first uses it on the 26th day of the income year", effective life
-- 3 1/3 years: "$3,500 x ([365 - 25] / 365) x (100% / 3 1/3) = $978". Unrounded, 3,500 x 340 x 3 / (365 x 10) = 3,570,000 / 3,650
-- = 978.08...; the Example prints it to the dollar.
#ASSERT `What is the decline in value by the prime cost method` 3500 340 (10 DIVIDED BY 3) 3500 EQUALS 3570000 DIVIDED BY 3650
#ASSERT FLOOR (`What is the decline in value by the prime cost method` 3500 340 (10 DIVIDED BY 3) 3500 PLUS 0.5) EQUALS 978
-- $10,000, a full year, 2 years' life: 5,000; limited to an opening adjustable value of $3,000: 3,000.
#ASSERT `What is the decline in value by the prime cost method` 10000 365 2 10000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `What is the decline in value by the prime cost method` 10000 365 2 3000 EQUALS 3000

§ `ss 40-70, 40-72 -- diminishing value`

-- Base value $10,000, a full year, 5 years: 200% / 5 = 40%, 4,000 (s 40-72); 150% / 5 = 30%, 3,000 (s 40-70).
#ASSERT `What is the decline in value by the diminishing value method` TRUE 10000 365 5 EQUALS 4000
#ASSERT `What is the decline in value by the diminishing value method` FALSE 10000 365 5 EQUALS 3000
-- 182 days: 10,000 x 182 x 200 / (365 x 100 x 5) = 3,640,000 / 1,825 = 1,994.52...
#ASSERT `What is the decline in value by the diminishing value method` TRUE 10000 182 5 EQUALS 3640000 DIVIDED BY 1825
-- A 1-year life gives 200%, which s 40-72(3) limits to the base value: 10,000.
#ASSERT `What is the decline in value by the diminishing value method` TRUE 10000 365 1 EQUALS 10000

§ `s 328-190(1) -- small business pool`

-- An opening pool balance of $20,000: 30% is 6,000.
#ASSERT `What can I deduct for my small business pool` 20000 EQUALS 6000
